// A LABELED DEFAULT IS BORN WITH THE BINDING (aug31f ryouko finding
// 01, design/wake_catchup.md): str::escape's `#esc = default_escape`
// reaches a fresh callee only as a STANDING store read, and the
// present-but-stale ruling (9b2e7231) stopped upgrading standing
// reads under an arm's wake view — so an instance born at a select
// arm's becoming-selected dispatch NEVER saw its config fire, the
// fired-gated seam never configured, and the arm emitted nothing,
// forever. BOTH engines broke together at those commits (the
// metamorphic blind spot — the differential oracle saw agreement);
// the interp side resurfaced alone once wake catch-up fixed the
// kernel's dispatch views. Fixes: the interp CallSite's bound
// dispatch seeds DEFAULT args FIRED (cycle-scoped, any depth — their
// one arrival is the instance's birth); the DynCallSlot's first
// dispatch is a BIRTH view (event.wake_init cleared — marshalled
// args keep their honest side-channel tags); and escape's config
// memo survives sleep (sleep is pause — clearing it demanded a fired
// re-delivery no wake provides).
// Expected: "\/foo\/bar" on both engines.
{let t = select i64:0 {i64:0 => str::escape("/foo/bar"), _ => null}; t}
